@@ -3,3 +3,24 @@
-JSON output preserves the records read from LF-separated input.
-Text output joins nonempty records with LF.
-Spaces in job names are data.
+This reference is for users of `render(input, format, token, expected)`.
+
+## Shared record semantics
+
+Text and JSON accept LF (`\n`) and CRLF (`\r\n`) record delimiters, including mixed input.
+Both formats omit empty records and preserve the order of all other records.
+Spaces in job names are data, including leading spaces, trailing spaces, and names made only of spaces.
+Names are not trimmed.
+A bare CR (`\r`) is data, not a delimiter, and remains in the name unless it is part of a CRLF delimiter.
+This applies inside a name and at the start or end of a name.
+
+## Output formats
+
+Text output joins the records with LF and does not add a final delimiter.
+JSON output returns the same records as a JSON array string, with normal JSON escaping for characters such as a bare CR.
+Empty input, or input that contains only delimiters, returns an empty string for text or `[]` for JSON.
+
+For example, input `" two \r\n\r\none\rname\n"` returns `" two \none\rname"` in text format.
+In JSON format, it returns the JSON text `[" two ","one\rname"]`.
+The examples use `\r` and `\n` to show CR and LF characters.
+
+Only `text` and `json` are supported formats. Other formats throw `Unknown format` after authorization succeeds.
+Authorization requires the exact token `Bearer <expected>`, with a nonempty string for `expected`, even for empty input.
+Invalid authorization throws `Unauthorized` before records are processed or a format is selected.
